      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T10:13:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, thanks for your reply. I fixed the build issue and added a test to clarify what I\u0027m trying to handle.\n\nThe basic fix is that now sshClient.Dial supports named ports (service names) like `ssh` or `https` instead of only numbers like `22` or `443`\n\nSome are defined here https://www.iana.org/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/service-names-port-numbers.xhtml\n\nThe net.Dial function supports this already as noted in the documentation https://pkg.go.dev/net#Dial, which means that ssh.Dial also supports this already https://pkg.go.dev/golang.org/x/crypto/ssh#Dial\n\nTo me it then seems like something was missed when sshClient.Dial does not support this same.",
      "parentUuid": "fed4052a_020f9368",
      "revId": "6df784d737cdd2f360969901e0ec731ce7aee6f5",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
