      "writtenOn": "2023-10-08T11:08:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the clarification and for the test case. My only concern is that `net.LookupPort` uses a background context and therefore may hang forever. For `ssh.Dial` we can pass a config with a timeout. We should have a way to pass a timeout or a context here too, but that requires an API change and so a proposal. In the meantime we could do something like this\n\n```\nctx, cancel :\u003d context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)\ndefer cancel()\n\nport, err :\u003d net.DefaultResolver.LookupPort(ctx, n, portString)\n```\n\n10 seconds should be more than enough here.\n\n@filippo@golang.org @hanwen@google.com what do you think about?",
      "parentUuid": "f202efea_15877655",
